From f3aec22c535e480c738cdd149eae9d25d81d8127 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Evinj <natively.contact@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 27 Aug 2026 03:46:52 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] @ chore(gitignore): ignore local AI-assistant and editor
 configs

.gemini/, .kiro/, .qoder/, .codebuddy/, GEMINI.md, QODER.md,
CODEBUDDY.md and opencode.jsonc are written by whichever assistant or
editor a given developer happens to run. None is part of the build, and
all of them showed up as untracked noise in every `git status`, which is
how real untracked work gets overlooked.

CLAUDE.md is deliberately NOT ignored: it is the shared, reviewed
cross-platform contract for this repo, not one person local tool state.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01K9YNdVhkUKsxnY6HLh1pbd
@
---
 .gitignore | 14 ++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+)

diff --git a/.gitignore b/.gitignore
index 5547fc77..bb81f1a8 100644
--- a/.gitignore
+++ b/.gitignore
@@ -539,3 +539,17 @@ benchmark-results/
 /natively_debug.size*
 /pitch/
 /researc
+
+# Local AI-assistant / editor configs. Each of these is written by a tool a
+# single developer happens to run (Gemini, Kiro, Qoder, CodeBuddy, opencode);
+# none of them is part of the build, and they otherwise show up as untracked
+# noise in every `git status`. CLAUDE.md is deliberately NOT here — it is the
+# shared, reviewed contract for this repo, not one person's local tool state.
+/.gemini/
+/.kiro/
+/.qoder/
+/.codebuddy/
+/GEMINI.md
+/QODER.md
+/CODEBUDDY.md
+/opencode.jsonc
-- 
